# Line endings, pinned.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows machine rewrites checked-out text to CRLF.
# build.js used to match a four-script block joined with \n, so after a fresh
# checkout the match silently failed and the build aborted with "external
# references remain". Tolerant matching now handles both, but a checkout whose
# endings depend on each collaborator's git config also turns every re-clone
# into whole-file diffs. Pinning text to LF makes the tree the same everywhere.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.html text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.wl   text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
